    "upstream_operation": "sigGen (d, message, k -> r, s)",
    "local_operation": "C_CreateObject(CKO_PRIVATE_KEY, CKK_EC, CKA_VALUE = d) and CKO_PUBLIC_KEY (04||qx||qy), C_Sign(CKM_ECDSA_<hash>) of the upstream message, then (a) C_Verify with the NIST public key (functional round-trip) and (b) an independent verifier (@noble/curves) over the same signature (independent oracle); r, s are not compared",
    "transformation": "subset; the upstream k, r and s are dropped; every retained field is byte-copied",
    "subset_policy": "Deterministic. P-256/384/521 x the eight hashes with a PKCS#11 v3.2 CKM_ECDSA_<hash> mechanism (SHA2-224/256/384/512, SHA3-224/256/384/512), plain (non-conformance, non-component) groups: the lowest tcId. Only the group key (d, qx, qy) and the message are carried: the upstream k, r and s are NOT carried — k is the signer's secret nonce and C_Sign draws its own, so r, s cannot be reproduced.",
    "retained_fields": "group: tgId, curve, hashAlg, d, qx, qy; case: tcId, message (k, r, s and deferred dropped)",
    "evidence_note": "The cases are recorded as functional-round-trip, not NIST reference samples: the NIST file supplies the key and message only; no NIST expected output is checked.",
    "test_only_key_material": "d values are public NIST ACVP-Server sample data, imported as session objects (CKA_TOKEN=false) and destroyed after the case"
  },
